course: dictionary
lesson: 12988
title: Experimentation: testing ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Experimentation is the word for trying things out to test ideas and find things out. Scientists do it, but so do cooks, artists and musicians. The word comes from experiment (to try something out), and the ending -ation turns it into a noun, the name of the whole process.
explain: «The class spent a week on experimentation: they tested which paper towel soaked up the most water.» The children were testing ideas, so experimentation means the whole process of testing, not just one test.
explain: Experimentation can also mean trying new and different ways of doing things to see what works. «Her cake recipe improved after weeks of experimentation with different flours.» She tried new things and kept what worked. Clues like «trying», «testing» or «new ideas» help you spot this meaning.
fact: Experimentation means the process of trying out experiments to test ideas.
fact: Experimentation can also mean trying new and different ways of doing things to see what works.
fact: Scientists use experimentation: they ask a question, make a prediction, test it fairly, measure and then decide what the results show.
fact: «Scientific experimentation» means testing ideas in science in a careful, fair way.
fact: «Animal experimentation» is a topic people argue about, because they have different views on it.
exercise: «The science class spent a week on experimentation with plants and water.» What does experimentation mean here? | *Trying out tests to find things out | Painting pictures of plants | Eating lunch in the canteen | Sleeping in the sun
exercise: Mia tried new ways to make her cookies, changing one thing at a time. Which word names what she was doing? | celebration | *experimentation | hesitation | decoration
exercise: Which phrase means testing ideas in science in a careful, fair way? | Sunny weather | *Scientific experimentation | Silent reading | Morning register
test: «Through experimentation, the artist found that thick paint dried faster.» What does experimentation most likely mean here? | Selling the paintings | Cleaning the brushes | *Trying different ways to find out what works | Copying another painting
test: Which word is the noun form of experiment? | *experimentation | experimented | experimental | exactly
exam: Which sentence uses experimentation correctly? | Experimentation ran to the shop. | She experimentation the door open quickly. | *The scientists used experimentation to test whether the new medicine worked. | The experimentation was blue and sang loudly.
